Stores all currencies used in the system with their symbols, rounding, and exchange rates for multi-currency transactions and reporting.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Multi-currency accounting, sales, purchases, and payments
Automatic or manual exchange rate updates
Currency conversion in journal entries, invoices, bank statements, and reports
Price lists and product pricing in foreign currencies
Bank accounts and payment reconciliation in foreign currency
Financial reporting (P&L, Balance Sheet) with currency translation
Localization and legal reporting requirements

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent, core)
Key Fields:
name (char, e.g. "USD"), symbol, full_name
rounding (float, usually 0.01), decimal_places
active, position (before/after)
rate_ids → One2many to res.currency.rate
company_id (for company-specific currencies)
Computed: rate (current rate vs company currency)

Critical Hooks: _compute_rate, compute, _get_conversion_rate, rate update wizards
Security: Usually read access for all users, write restricted to accounting managers

RAG Routing Keywords:
currency, res.currency, exchange rate, foreign currency, multi currency, currency rate, base currency, company currency, rate update, currency conversion, USD, EUR, IDR, forex rate
Related Models (most joined):

res.currency.rate (child rates — most important)
res.company (currency_id)
account.move, account.move.line (currency_id, amount_currency)
account.payment, pos.order, sale.order
product.pricelist

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
res.currency is Odoo’s core currency model storing name, symbol, rounding, position, and current exchange rates. It enables multi-currency operations across accounting, sales, purchase, inventory, and POS, with automatic conversion, rate history via res.currency.rate, and is referenced on almost every monetary document and report in the system.